        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Fragment of a chasuble, woven silk, China, 16th century"@en , "Given by Monsieur S. Baron"@en , "Portion fachasuble of green satin, woven in yellow silk, with rows of circles, united by small dotted hands; each of the circles contains another circle, enclosing four <i>fleurs-de-lys</i> and surrounded by scrollwork and a dotted band. The interspaces  occupied by floral crosses, with rosettes in the centre."@en ;
